{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the man took a golden ring and two bracelets for her hands</b> — This verse lacks the action, for it should have said: \"And the man took a golden ring and placed it on her nose, and two bracelets on her hands.\" Therefore I say that its meaning is: \"And the man took a golden ring and two bracelets that would be on her hands,\" and he said to her, \"Whose daughter are you?\" And after she said to him, \"I am the daughter of Bethuel,\" he placed the ring on her nose and the bracelets on her hands, as he told them (later). But the act of giving is omitted here, and so too in many places."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:34:17.789935185Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}